# Line-ending policy — added 2026-08-01.
#
# Why this exists: Alphab2bapp and its forks (markup_app, moneyman_app,
# marketanalysis_app, zamzam_app, Kaizen_app) are separate repos seeded from
# snapshots of each other, so keeping them in sync means diffing working trees
# directly. Editor-introduced CRLF made files that are byte-identical in git
# look like large diffs — `PendingOrderWarningModal.js` and
# `ReconciliationService.js` each showed as fully-rewritten (627 and 436 lines)
# during the 2026-08-01 fork comparison, purely from line endings.
#
# `core.autocrlf=input` already normalises on commit, so nothing wrong ever
# reached git; this makes checkout write LF too, so the working tree stops
# drifting and cross-repo comparisons stay honest.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.webp  binary
*.pdf   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks   binary
*.p12   binary
*.mobileprovision binary

# Windows-native tooling that expects CRLF.
*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
